
-- Batch 7: Indian, Iranian, Italian, Ivory Coast, Japan, Kenya recipes
UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Cauliflower Steaks with Turmeric celebrate India''s 5,000-year love affair with turmeric, known as "the golden spice." Used in Ayurvedic medicine for millennia, turmeric represents India''s profound connection between food and healing. This modern preparation bridges ancient Indian spice traditions with contemporary plant-based dining.' WHERE slug = 'cauliflower-steaks-in';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Golden Milk (Haldi Doodh) is an ancient Indian Ayurvedic remedy combining turmeric with warm milk. This healing beverage has been used in Indian households for thousands of years to boost immunity and reduce inflammation. Its recent Western popularity as a "superfood latte" reflects India''s global culinary influence.' WHERE slug = 'golden-milk-in';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Masala Chai is India''s most beloved beverage, a spiced tea combining black tea with cardamom, ginger, cinnamon, and cloves in sweetened milk. Chai culture dates back to the British introduction of tea plantations in the 1830s, but Indians transformed it into something uniquely their own through the addition of traditional spices.' WHERE slug = 'masala-chai-in';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Naan bread has ancient roots in the Persian Empire and was brought to the Indian subcontinent by the Mughals. The word "naan" comes from Persian for bread. Traditionally baked in a tandoor clay oven, naan has been a staple of North Indian cuisine since the 16th century Mughal era.' WHERE slug = 'naan-bread-in';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'The Samosa has traveled from its origins as the Persian "sanbosag" across Central Asia to India, where it became one of the world''s most popular snacks. Indian samosas, filled with spiced potatoes and peas, have been documented since the 13th century Delhi Sultanate and are now enjoyed globally.' WHERE slug = 'samosa-in';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Chicken Tikka Masala is one of the most popular dishes worldwide, blending tandoori chicken with a creamy tomato-based sauce. Whether it originated in Punjab or Glasgow, it represents the beautiful fusion of Indian and British culinary traditions that emerged through centuries of cultural exchange.' WHERE slug = 'chicken-tikka-masala-india';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Chicken Tikka Masala bridges Indian and British culinary cultures. The tandoori chicken tradition dates to ancient India, while the creamy tomato sauce reflects both Mughlai cooking and British adaptation. This beloved dish symbolizes how migration and cultural exchange create extraordinary new cuisines.' WHERE slug = 'chicken-tikka-masala';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Easy Chickpea Curry represents the intersection of Indian and British home cooking. Chickpea curry has roots in India''s ancient vegetarian traditions, where legumes have been cultivated for over 7,000 years. The "easy" adaptation reflects how Indian flavors have been embraced in British everyday cooking.' WHERE slug = 'easy-chickpea-curry';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Pistachio Rosewater Cake showcases Iran''s centuries-old tradition of combining pistachios and rosewater in desserts. Iran is the world''s second-largest pistachio producer, and rosewater distillation originated in Persia over 1,000 years ago. This elegant cake represents the refinement of Persian pastry traditions.' WHERE slug = 'pistachio-cake-ir';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Asia', history = 'Shirazi Salad is a classic Iranian salad named after the city of Shiraz, a center of Persian culture and poetry. This simple combination of diced cucumbers, tomatoes, and onions with lime juice and mint embodies the Persian love of fresh, vibrant flavors and has been a staple of Iranian tables for centuries.' WHERE slug = 'shirazi-salad-ir';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Arancini are Sicilian rice balls that date to the 10th century Arab rule of Sicily when rice cultivation was introduced. These golden-fried spheres stuffed with ragù and cheese were originally a portable meal for workers and travelers. Today they''re Sicily''s most celebrated street food.' WHERE slug = 'arancini-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Bruschetta traces to ancient Rome where it was used to test the quality of freshly pressed olive oil. The word comes from "bruscare" meaning to roast over coals. This simple preparation of grilled bread with tomatoes, garlic, and basil celebrates the Italian philosophy of letting quality ingredients shine.' WHERE slug = 'bruschetta-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Lentil and Kale Soup reflects Italy''s ancient tradition of cucina povera (peasant cooking). Lentils have been cultivated in Italy since Roman times, symbolizing prosperity and good fortune. This hearty soup represents the Italian genius of transforming humble ingredients into deeply satisfying meals.' WHERE slug = 'lentil-kale-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Farro salad celebrates one of Italy''s oldest grains, cultivated since Roman times. Farro was the staple grain of Roman legions and was used as currency. This Mediterranean preparation with fresh vegetables and herbs showcases how ancient grains are being rediscovered in modern Italian cuisine.' WHERE slug = 'farro-salad-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Focaccia is one of Italy''s oldest breads, with origins predating the Roman Empire. The Ligurian version, drizzled with olive oil and rosemary, represents the simplicity of Italian baking. Focaccia has been made in Italian homes and bakeries for over 2,000 years, with each region developing its own style.' WHERE slug = 'focaccia-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Panna Cotta ("cooked cream") is a silky Italian dessert from Piedmont. While its exact origins are debated, the modern version emerged in the 1960s. This elegant dessert of sweetened cream set with gelatin represents the Italian mastery of simple ingredients transformed into refined culinary experiences.' WHERE slug = 'panna-cotta-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Prosciutto-Wrapped Melon combines the saltiness of Italian dry-cured ham with sweet cantaloupe—a classic Italian antipasto. Prosciutto production in Italy dates back over 2,000 years to Roman times. This pairing exemplifies the Italian philosophy of contrasting flavors creating perfect harmony.' WHERE slug = 'prosciutto-melon-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Risotto alla Milanese is Milan''s signature dish, a saffron-infused rice preparation dating to 1574 when a glassworker''s apprentice added saffron to his master''s wedding risotto. The dish showcases Northern Italy''s rice-growing Po Valley heritage and the precious saffron traded along medieval spice routes.' WHERE slug = 'risotto-milanese-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Stuffed Artichokes (Carciofi alla Romana) are a Roman tradition dating back to the Jewish community of Rome''s ancient ghetto. Artichokes were prized by the Romans and have been a Mediterranean diet staple for over 2,500 years. This preparation reflects Rome''s rich vegetable cooking traditions.' WHERE slug = 'stuffed-artichokes-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Tiramisu is Italy''s most famous dessert, with debated origins claimed by both Veneto and Friuli-Venezia Giulia in the 1960s-1970s. The name means "pick me up" or "lift me up," referencing the energizing espresso and cocoa. This layered dessert of mascarpone, ladyfingers, and coffee has conquered the world.' WHERE slug = 'tiramisu-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Tomato Basil Soup is an Italian classic that celebrates the introduction of tomatoes from the Americas in the 16th century. Initially feared as poisonous by Europeans, tomatoes became central to Italian cuisine by the 18th century. This simple soup embodies the Italian reverence for seasonal, quality ingredients.' WHERE slug = 'tomato-basil-it';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Baked Feta Pasta went viral on TikTok in 2021 from Finnish food blogger Jenni Häyrinen. The recipe of baking feta cheese with tomatoes then tossing with pasta became one of the most searched recipes ever. It represents how social media transforms simple home cooking into global phenomena.' WHERE slug = 'baked-feta-pasta';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Spaghetti Aglio e Olio is a cornerstone of Italian cucina povera—peasant cooking that transforms the simplest pantry staples (garlic, olive oil, chili) into something extraordinary. This Roman and Neapolitan classic proves that Italian genius lies not in complexity but in perfecting simplicity.' WHERE slug = 'spaghetti-aglio-olio-green-olives';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Europe', history = 'Venetian Mac and Cheese blends the Italian pasta tradition with American comfort food sensibilities. Venice''s maritime trade history brought diverse ingredients and cooking techniques to the lagoon city. This fusion dish reflects the ongoing culinary conversation between Italian and American food cultures.' WHERE slug = 'venetian-mac-and-cheese';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Alloco is a beloved Ivorian street food of deep-fried ripe plantains, typically served with spicy pepper sauce and grilled fish. This dish represents the importance of plantains in West African cuisine and the vibrant street food culture of Abidjan, Ivory Coast''s largest city.' WHERE slug = 'alloco';
